WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.308 --> 00:00:02.189
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:02.189 --> 00:00:04.011
- Imagine two acres of land

00:00:04.011 --> 00:00:07.821
that are covered with Las Vegas history,

00:00:07.821 --> 00:00:11.360
dating from the 1930s up to present day,

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.693
and when you walk in, they tell a story.

00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:20.980
The Neon Museum was founded
in 1996, and we rescue signs.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:26.599
There are over 200 signs
in the Neon boneyard.

00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:29.770
Las Vegas is a town that
is known for imploding

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.839
all of its hotels and not
preserving its history

00:00:31.839 --> 00:00:33.059
because we're always wanting to move on

00:00:33.059 --> 00:00:36.226
to the bigger, better, brighter thing.

00:00:37.279 --> 00:00:40.029
There's beauty in the worn signs.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.500
They're a glimpse into the past.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.271
You see that rusted paint.

00:00:44.271 --> 00:00:48.740
You see the broken neon, and
it's kind of bittersweet.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.410
The folks who designed these
are really master craftsmen.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.730
They hand-blowed the neon that's in them.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.650
The Yucca Motel, the intricate
artwork, the glass blowing

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.399
that had to go into the
design of the actual Yucca,

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:04.231
the Stardust spire
reaching up into the sky.

00:01:04.231 --> 00:01:07.814
It's becoming a art
form that's going away.

00:01:09.011 --> 00:01:10.722
We preserve a lot of those memories

00:01:10.722 --> 00:01:13.591
so people who didn't see the
signs actually on the strip

00:01:13.591 --> 00:01:15.183
are able to come here and get a real sense

00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:18.016
for what they were like in person.

